  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. All component choices in config_039 are supported by ablations: scvi_n200 > scgpt > pca for RNA, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50 for image, multiprofile > singleprofile, transformer > avgpool, and weighted > concat (0.7131 vs 0.6878 with resnet50). Question: config_038 is identical to config_039 except it uses concat fusion instead of weighted. While weighted outperformed concat by ~0.025 with resnet50, the interaction with the stronger imagenet_vit_l backbone could shift the balance—concat might preserve complementary information that weighted averaging dilutes. Why this is the best use of the final experiment: With 0 experiments remaining, exploitation is paramount. config_038 shares 5 of 6 design axes with the current best and is the highest-expected-value untested configuration. All other remaining options swap the RNA encoder to scgpt or pca (both substantially worse in RNA-only) or drop to singleprofile, making them very unlikely to exceed 0.7250. config_038 offers the best (albeit modest) chance of a small improvement or at minimum a clean confirmation of the optimal fusion strategy."
